# Architecture

## Overview

{{ project_name }} is a TypeScript CLI application using commander.

## Project Structure

```
src/
  index.ts               # CLI entry point (commander)
  config.ts              # zod-based env/config validation
  logging.ts             # pino setup
  commands/              # CLI subcommands
    example.ts           # Example command
  services/              # Business logic
{%- if include_clients %}
  clients/               # External API/service clients
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
  db.ts                  # Prisma client setup
  repositories/          # Data access layer
{%- endif %}
tests/
  unit/                  # Fast, isolated unit tests
  integration/           # Tests with real dependencies
  e2e/                   # End-to-end tests
```

## Flow

```
CLI commands (parse args, call services)
  -> services (business logic)
{%- if include_clients %}
    -> clients (external API calls)
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
    -> repositories (data access via Prisma)
{%- endif %}
```

## Toolchain

| Tool | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| Bun | Runtime and package manager |
| TypeScript | Type system |
| Biome | Formatting and linting |
| bun test | Testing |
| commander | CLI framework |
| chalk | Terminal styling |
| pino | Structured logging |
| zod | Config/env validation |
{%- if include_database %}
| Prisma | ORM and database access |
{%- endif %}

## Conventions

- All configuration is in `package.json` and `tsconfig.json`.
- Version is the single source of truth in `package.json`.
- Commands are thin I/O wrappers; business logic lives in services.
- Input/Output types use zod schemas.
